      "parents": [
        {
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bitcoin/bitcoin/git/commits/228877d7836a55c1d6fde90b0b7ba2d4c90248ab",
          "sha": "228877d7836a55c1d6fde90b0b7ba2d4c90248ab",
          "html_url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/commit/228877d7836a55c1d6fde90b0b7ba2d4c90248ab"
        }
      ],
      "message": "net: remember addresses of recent inbound connection attempts\n\nAdd two rolling bloom filters to CConnman that record which addresses\n(IPv6: which /48s) made inbound connection attempts in the current and\nthe previous INBOUND_RECONNECT_WINDOW (10 minutes). The filters are\nswapped once a window has passed, so an address is remembered for\nbetween one and two windows after its last attempt and then forgotten.\nIf more than two windows pass without any attempt, both filters are\ncleared.\n\nNoteInboundAttempt() records an attempt and reports whether the same\nkey made at least two attempts within that time. The threshold is two\nrather than one so that a single honest retry is never counted: a peer\nwhose first connection was closed before it received anything retries\nonce with v1 (V2Transport::ShouldReconnectV1), and a node that restarts\nreconnects once. An address that connects three times in twenty\nminutes is not doing either. It is not used yet.\n\nIPv6 is keyed by /48 because the entity this targets controls a whole\n/48 and could otherwise use a fresh address per attempt. Honest nodes\nsharing a /48 are lumped together; in practice that is rare (a day of\ninbound traffic on a busy node showed 60 distinct /48s carrying 64\ndistinct /64s) and it only matters while the node is full.\n\nSince the filters can't count, each key uses two entries: key+1 after\nthe first attempt and key+2 after the second. Entries are only inserted\nwhen not already present: every insert counts towards the filter's own\ngeneration rollover, and an address that retries every second must not\npush the others out.",
      "committer": {
