          "html_url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/commit/1cb8fa55e15a751d213df3a06d722fa389b58802"
        }
      ],
      "message": "net: drop recent reconnects instead of evicting when inbound slots are full\n\nWhen an inbound connection arrives from an address that already made\ntwo attempts within the last one to two INBOUND_RECONNECT_WINDOWs and\nall inbound slots are taken, drop the new connection instead of\nevicting an existing peer for it. If a slot is free the connection is\naccepted as before, so this is not a ban: it only decides who gives\nway when we are full.\n\nThis targets entities that open many short-lived inbound connections\nand reconnect within a second of being disconnected. On a full node\nevery such attempt evicted an existing peer, which is almost always\nthe youngest one, i.e. an honest peer that connected a moment ago.\n\nInbound Tor connections (which all come from the local Tor proxy),\nlocal addresses in general and NoBan peers are not tracked. The\ntest-only option -test=inbound_reconnect_check_local applies the check\nto local addresses so that the functional tests, which connect from\n127.0.0.1, can exercise it.\n\nThe result is stored in CNode::m_recent_reconnect for use by the\ntx-relay capacity check in net_processing.",
      "committer": {
        "name": "0xb10c",
        "email": "github@b10c.me",
        "date": "2026-10-17T15:31:11Z"
      },
      "author": {
        "name": "0xb10c",
        "email": "github@b10c.me",
        "date": "2026-10-17T11:18:06Z"
      },
