        }
      ],
      "message": "p2p: drop recent reconnects instead of evicting when tx-relay slots are full\n\nWith -inboundrelaypercent, a new inbound peer that relays transactions\ncan evict an existing tx-relaying inbound peer when it sends its\nversion message (or later, when it switches to tx relay with\nfilterload/filterclear). On nodes with default settings the tx-relay\nslots fill long before the overall inbound limit, so this is where\nreconnecting entities evict the most peers.\n\nApply the same rule as in CreateNodeFromAcceptedSocket: if the address\nof the new peer connected recently, drop the new peer when the\ntx-relay slots are full, instead of evicting an existing one.\n\nSplit CConnman::EvictTxPeerIfFull() into InboundTxRelayFull() and the\neviction attempt so that the capacity check can be used on its own.",
      "committer": {
        "name": "0xb10c",
        "email": "github@b10c.me",
        "date": "2026-10-17T15:31:12Z"
      },
      "author": {
        "name": "0xb10c",
        "email": "github@b10c.me",
        "date": "2026-10-17T11:20:50Z"
      },
      "sha": "9f6a312d1a70e4ad5d8227ba69fa9938f988d1d3"
    },
